        "Harald Rose",
        "Knut Urban",
        "Maximilian Haider"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration correction overcame a central limit in electron microscopy and enabled routine sub-angstrom imaging, opening new experimental access to atomic structure and materials.",
        "attribution": "Rose's optical designs, Haider's realization of practical correctors, and Urban's work demonstrating their impact on materials research represent distinct, complementary contributions.",
        "maturity": "The method has been independently adopted and developed over decades, with clear and lasting scientific impact.",
        "uncertainties": [
