        "Isao Tanihata",
        "Björn Jonson"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The discovery of neutron halo nuclei exposed unexpected spatial structure in weakly bound nuclei and changed experimental and theoretical approaches to exotic nuclear matter.",
        "attribution": "Tanihata's measurements established the anomalously large reaction cross sections; Jonson and collaborators developed the halo interpretation and its experimental program.",
        "maturity": "Halo structure has been confirmed across multiple nuclei and methods, making this a mature nuclear-physics result.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery and interpretation were collaborative, and the distinction between first observation and conceptual identification needs to be made explicit."
        ]
      }
    },
